{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>There is</b> — <b>ransom</b>: two joined together." "<b>Makes himself rich</b> — who rises to wealth and had nothing at all." "<b>And becomes poor</b> — who returns to being poor, though he had much money. And this one has no advantage over that one, for the rich man — if he is seized on account of his money — gives wealth as the ransom of his life, but the poor man does not hear the rebuke of an officer or taskmaster."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:31.204989339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}